		{"id":"4db2b6a63df1bb5b","x":-900,"y":-40,"width":544,"height":356,"color":"1","type":"text","text":"Mindmaps:\n\n- Different Types\n\t- Concepts\n\t\t- Internal/External Notes\n\t- Cultural\n\t\t- Examples\n\t\t- Studies\n\t\t- Quotes\n\t\t- Names\n\t\t- Ages\n\t- Feynman: Helper to tell the topic to someone else\n\t\t- Index for a moc"},
		{"id":"1ad267537eecaaff","x":-900,"y":340,"width":544,"height":240,"type":"text","text":"Perfect Book annotations:\n\n1. U can go back to the source\n2. All the important things are extracted (not really need to go back to the book)\n3. "},
		{"id":"4358da748feab92c","x":-900,"y":600,"width":544,"height":160,"type":"text","text":"Annotation Clean automation\n\n- Bullet Points summaries\n- Categorization\n- Placement and link\n- Movement to obsidian"},
		{"id":"2c0779d679a1bf15","x":-569,"y":824,"width":969,"height":1156,"type":"text","text":"| Reading situation                           | What must be preserved?                                                                                                  |\n| ------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |\n| A memorable quotation                       | Exact wording, source location, and why it matters                                                                       |\n| A technical definition                      | Precise definition, explanation, and an example                                                                          |\n| A complex argument                          | Conclusion, premises, reasoning, evidence, and caveats                                                                   |\n| A historical event                          | What happened, relevant context, and causal explanation                                                                  |\n| An idea you disagree with                   | Author's claim, supporting argument, and your objection                                                                  |\n| An unresolved question                      | The question, its context, and possible connections                                                                      |\n| A concept appearing in several books        | Distinct sources and the relationships between their explanations                                                        |\n| A mathematical definition                   | Formal definition, notation, assumptions, domain of validity, and an intuitive interpretation                            |\n| A mathematical theorem                      | Formal statement, hypotheses, conclusion, and conditions under which it applies                                          |\n| A mathematical proof                        | Main proof strategy, key steps, dependencies, and the reasoning behind non-obvious transitions                           |\n| A mathematical derivation                   | Starting assumptions, transformations, intermediate results, and final expression                                        |\n| A mathematical formula                      | Formula, meaning of each variable, assumptions, units where applicable, and a practical example                          |\n| A mathematical technique                    | When to use it, why it works, procedure, limitations, and a representative problem                                       |\n| A worked mathematical problem               | Problem statement, solution strategy, critical steps, result, and lessons that generalize to other problems              |\n| A mathematical intuition                    | Informal explanation, visual or geometric interpretation, connection to formal results, and limitations of the intuition |\n| A mathematical counterexample               | Claim being challenged, counterexample, and the reason it invalidates the claim                                          |\n| An economic concept                         | Definition, underlying mechanism, assumptions, implications, and a real-world example                                    |\n| An economic model                           | Purpose, assumptions, variables, relationships, predictions, and limitations                                             |\n| An economic theory                          | Main claims, causal mechanisms, supporting arguments, competing explanations, and scope of applicability                 |\n| An economic equation                        | Formula, variable definitions, economic interpretation, assumptions, and implications when variables change              |\n| A causal economic relationship              | Proposed cause-and-effect mechanism, direction of causality, conditions, confounding factors, and supporting evidence    |\n| A macroeconomic indicator                   | Definition, measurement method, interpretation, relevant time horizon, and limitations                                   |\n| An economic empirical finding               | Research question, data, methodology, key results, uncertainty, and limitations on generalization                        |\n| An economic policy proposal                 | Objective, intervention mechanism, expected benefits, costs, distributional effects, and unintended consequences         |\n| An economic historical episode              | Context, sequence of events, relevant institutions, proposed causal explanations, and competing interpretations          |\n| An economic debate                          | Main positions, underlying assumptions, strongest arguments, supporting evidence, and unresolved disagreements           |\n| A financial instrument or market mechanism  | Structure, cash flows, pricing logic, risks, relevant assumptions, and practical use                                     |\n| A software design principle                 | Problem addressed, principle, rationale, when it applies, trade-offs, and situations where it may be inappropriate       |\n| A software architecture                     | Components, responsibilities, dependencies, data flow, key design decisions, and quality attributes addressed            |\n| A design pattern                            | Problem, proposed solution, structure, consequences, appropriate use cases, and alternatives                             |\n| A software algorithm                        | Problem solved, inputs and outputs, core idea, steps, complexity, assumptions, and edge cases                            |\n| A data structure                            | Organization of data, supported operations, time and space complexity, invariants, and appropriate use cases             |\n| A programming language feature              | Syntax, semantics, intended use, examples, edge cases, and differences from similar features                             |\n| An API or library                           | Purpose, key interfaces, expected inputs and outputs, usage example, constraints, and common pitfalls                    |\n| A code example                              | Essential implementation, explanation of non-obvious parts, dependencies, expected behavior, and limitations             |\n| A software engineering technique            | Problem addressed, workflow, rationale, prerequisites, trade-offs, and conditions for success                            |\n| A debugging technique                       | Symptoms addressed, diagnostic reasoning, steps, root cause, and how to recognize similar problems                       |\n| A testing strategy                          | What is being tested, relevant test level, test design, expected behavior, limitations, and failure modes                |\n| A performance optimization                  | Original bottleneck, proposed change, measured improvement, measurement conditions, and trade-offs                       |\n| A software security principle               | Threat addressed, underlying vulnerability, mitigation, assumptions, and residual risks                                  |\n| A software failure or incident              | Context, triggering conditions, root cause, contributing factors, impact, resolution, and preventive measures            |\n| A technical comparison                      | Alternatives, evaluation criteria, relevant constraints, trade-offs, and conditions favoring each option                 |\n| A software project case study               | Context, requirements, decisions, implementation, outcomes, lessons learned, and applicability elsewhere                 |\n| An implementation-specific detail           | Relevant version or environment, configuration, constraints, and whether the detail is likely to change                  |\n| A concept appearing in multiple disciplines | Meaning in each context, shared principles, important differences, and limits of the analogy                             |"},
		{"id":"536baf3d4f18fe66","x":-218,"y":300,"width":638,"height":380,"type":"text","text":"### Dimension A — Knowledge structure\n\nWhat kind of information is this?\n\nConcept · Claim · Reasoning · Procedure · Evidence · Reference\n\n### Dimension B — Domain\n\nWhat subject does it belong to?\n\nMathematics · Economics · Software · Physics · History\n\n### Dimension C — Knowledge relationships\n\nHow does it relate to other information?\n\nSupports · Explains · Derives · Contradicts · Applies · Exemplifies"}
	],
	"edges":[
		{"id":"5057b33f78d05360","fromNode":"acd6a21c57fa2cd3","fromSide":"right","toNode":"938f662d05025704","toSide":"left","label":"Comentarios"}
	]
}